---
import ToolLayout from "../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro";
import { LengthConverter } from "../../../components/converters/LengthConverter.js";
import { getToolByPath } from "../../../content/tools.js";

const tool = getToolByPath("/tools/converters/length")!;
---

<ToolLayout
  tool={tool}
  purpose="Length converter for centimeters, inches, feet, meters, yards, miles, and millimeters."
>
  <LengthConverter client:load />

  <Fragment slot="details">
    <h2>Common length conversions</h2>
    <table>
      <caption>Length factors used by this converter</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">From</th>
          <th scope="col">Equals</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>1 inch</td>
          <td>2.54 centimeters</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>1 centimeter</td>
          <td>0.393701 inches (rounded)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>1 foot</td>
          <td>0.3048 meters</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>1 meter</td>
          <td>3.28084 feet (rounded)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>1 mile</td>
          <td>1.609344 kilometers</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Every unit is converted through meters as a common base (e.g. 1 inch = 0.0254 meters, per the international
      yard-and-pound agreement), then from meters into your target unit. This two-step approach keeps every
      conversion pair mathematically consistent. Surface measurements use the
      <a href="/tools/converters/area/">area converter</a> instead.
    </p>

    <h2>Accepted inputs</h2>
    <p>
      One number and any two of millimeter, centimeter, meter, kilometer, inch, foot, yard, and mile. The converter
      opens on 1 meter to feet. Zero stays zero.
    </p>

    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      The opening conversion, 1 meter to feet, displays 3.28084 feet. That figure is the six-decimal display of 1 ÷
      0.3048 (about 3.280839895…). Ten miles is exactly 16.09344 kilometers. One inch is exactly 2.54 centimeters.
    </p>

    <h2>How to read the result</h2>
    <p>
      The converter shows at most six decimal places. Exact definitions such as 1 inch = 0.0254 meters and 1 foot =
      0.3048 meters are used internally. Displayed values derived from those factors, including 3.28084 feet per meter
      and 0.393701 inches per centimeter, are rounded and are not a second set of exact factors.
    </p>

    <h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Base conversion factors follow standard SI and customary definitions (for example, 1 inch = 0.0254 meters and 1 foot = 0.3048 meters exactly).</li>
      <li>Results are rounded for display to six decimal places. A rounded display value is not itself an exact conversion factor.</li>
      <li>Very large or very small values may show fewer significant digits because of floating-point limits in JavaScript numbers.</li>
      <li>This converts length only. For acres, square feet, or other areas, use the <a href="/tools/converters/area/">area converter</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reference</h2>
    <p>
      Conversion factors follow NIST Special Publication 811 (<em>Guide for the Use of the International System of
      Units</em>) and NIST Handbook 44, the standard references for SI and customary unit conversions in the US.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
